// The black smoker — a vent that actually vents.
//
// `the_vent.ron` is a slide with one small sun at the bottom of it and nothing else: the vent is
// a *light* source, and its own header admits that a chloroplast near a vent and a chloroplast
// in daylight run the same reaction on a different intensity. This is the other half — a vent
// that puts matter into the water as well as light, which is what a real one does and what
// `Scenario::flux` was built for.
//
// Sulphide wells up at the mouth and washes out over the rim. It is not decoration: pathway 2
// of the default metabolic chemistry burns sulphide against the same oxidant as the others, so
// this is a genuine second economy, in the water, unused.
//
// **Nothing shipped in `genomes/` can eat it.** Every one of them runs a mitochondrion on its
// default control word, which selects pathway 0 and burns sugar. Reaching the sulphide takes one
// `OSET` writing 2 into `control[1]` of an organelle that already exists — one instruction, on a
// value a copy error can land on by itself. That is the experiment.
//
// The light is `the_vent.ron`'s exactly, and that is the design: this and the vent differ in the
// plume and in nothing else, so the pair is a control the way `archipelago` and
// `archipelago_control` are. Any difference in what evolves here is the sulphide's doing.
//
// Making the light meaner was tried first and is a dead end worth recording, because the
// interesting result would have been a population poor enough to *need* the sulphide. It does
// not survive being made poor. Over six thousand ticks, from sixteen founders:
//
//   intensity 4096, half-life 8  →  127, 587, 813   thriving
//   intensity 2048, half-life 8  →    7,   7,   7   persisting, never growing
//   intensity 3072, half-life 6  →    5,   5,   3   guttering
//   intensity 4096, half-life 5  →    2,   0,   0   extinct by four thousand
//
// The cliff is in the half-life and not the intensity: eight squares works and six does not,
// at any brightness tried. Which says the constraint is the *area* of the lit disc rather than
// how bright the middle of it is — a population needs room to be a population, and a small
// bright spot is a smaller habitat than a large dim one. A slide poor enough to make the
// sulphide urgent is a slide too poor to hold anything that might discover it.
//
//   mm-cli run scenarios/the_black_smoker.ron --ticks 500000 --archive smoker.ndjson
//
// What to watch is the trophic split in the budget pane. Income attributed to `influx` is energy
// that arrived latent in the sulphide; while every cell is photosynthesising it sits in the
// water, arrives, and washes straight back out over the rim. A run where the world's stored
// energy climbs against a flat light income is a run where something has started drinking.
(
    name: "the black smoker",
    seed: 20260804,
    width: 128,
    height: 128,

    // `the_vent.ron`'s light, unchanged, so the two scenarios are a matched pair.
    light: PointSource(
        x: 64,
        y: 64,
        intensity: 4096,
        half_life_squares: 8,
    ),

    // Convection off the mouth, which is what carries the plume outward. Without it the
    // sulphide would sit in the middle and diffuse into a bullseye.
    current: Rotational(strength: 64),
    fluid_interval: 1,

    seeding: [
        Uniform(chemical: 11, per_square: 409600),
        // The carbonate system (`docs/CHEMISTRY.md` §11). Carbonate matched to the dissolved
        // CO2 above, so the slide starts at pH 7 and every move from there is something the
        // cells did. Calcium is then *not* free: the pair precipitates on the product of the
        // two, so this is set to put `sqrt(calcium * carbonate)` a little over
        // `minerals.calcite_saturation` — near enough to equilibrium that the pH decides which
        // way it goes, which is the whole point of the coupling.
        Uniform(chemical: 18, per_square: 409600),
        Uniform(chemical: 17, per_square: 3461),
        Uniform(chemical: 14, per_square: 409600),
        Uniform(chemical: 4, per_square: 409600),
        // The three minerals nothing in the engine produces (`docs/CHEMISTRY.md` §8): seeding is
        // the only way in, and without them a nucleus, an enzyme or a shell cannot be built at
        // all. At the Redfield proportion of this world's own carbon — 16/106 nitrogen, 1/106
        // phosphorus rounded up — and half that again in silicon, matching the fresh slide.
        Uniform(chemical: 5, per_square: 61440),
        Uniform(chemical: 6, per_square: 4096),
        // The inert pool a diazosome cracks. Four times the bioavailable nitrogen: a
        // young world is mostly locked up, and unlocking it is what the organelle is for.
        Uniform(chemical: 16, per_square: 245760),
        Uniform(chemical: 7, per_square: 20480),
    ],

    inhabitants: [
        (genome: "ancestor.mm", count: 16),
    ],

    // The plume. A source at the mouth and four drains around the rim — a rectangle cannot be a
    // ring, and saying so in four lines is better than a shape nobody can picture.
    //
    // The drains are a rate rather than an amount, so the rim cannot scour the slide dry: what
    // leaves rises with what has reached the edge, and the standing plume settles where the two
    // meet. That level is the resource, and it is a number the vent's strength sets.
    flux: [
        Source(chemical: 10, x: 61, y: 61, width: 6, height: 6, per_tick: 24000),
        Drain(chemical: 10, x: 0, y: 0, width: 128, height: 4, rate: 64),
        Drain(chemical: 10, x: 0, y: 124, width: 128, height: 4, rate: 64),
        Drain(chemical: 10, x: 0, y: 4, width: 4, height: 120, rate: 64),
        Drain(chemical: 10, x: 124, y: 4, width: 4, height: 120, rate: 64),
    ],

    barriers: [],
)
